---
description: Slash commands /run /start /fix /stop for local API, admin-web, and Expo Metro
alwaysApply: true
---

When the user types `/run`, `/start`, `/fix`, or `/stop`, follow `.cursor/skills/dev-stack/SKILL.md` immediately.

**Stop latch:** `/stop` writes `.run/dev-stack.stopped`. While that file exists, `/run` and `/fix` must NOT start or restart API/admin/Metro. Only `/start` clears the latch and starts the stack. Check `bash .cursor/skills/dev-stack/scripts/stack.sh status` before spawning Shells.

- `/start`: clear latch + start missing API / admin / Metro as **three background Shells** (`block_until_ms: 0`)
- `/run`: if latched, refuse; else same three Shells as `/start`
- `/fix`: if latched, keep down; else restart only what is unhealthy
- `/stop`: `bash .cursor/skills/dev-stack/scripts/stack.sh stop` — free `:4000` `:3000` `:8081`, kill orphan shells, write latch
- Health: `bash .cursor/skills/dev-stack/scripts/stack.sh status`
- Do not ask first.
